visit temple in Kathmandu ", "text": "It is one of a must-visit temples in Kathmandu. If you’re lucky, you’ll get to see the cremation ceremony of dead people during your visit. \n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "8057F91E9EF7D520A2B45D34C3A7057A", "name": "Sendy H", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/SendyHermawati", "username": "SendyHermawati", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/51/92/2e/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 302, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294229, "location_name": "Jakarta", "location_name_detailed": "Jakarta, Indonesia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-01", "published_at_date": "2018-10-01"}, {"review_id": 620930192, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r620930192-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Half day", "text": "Pashupatinath lies on the banks of Bagmati River and this Hindu Temple precinct consists of temples, ashrams, inscriptions and images. Boudhanath area, which is just 5 mins drive away from Pashupatinath, is rich in Tibetan Culture within Kathmandu and is home to more than 50 Tibetan Monasteries (Gompas).", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2018-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "73E44C07F2D45D392E2A6107F025FE7A", "name": "Raju Khadka", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/RajuNRR", "username": "RajuNRR", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/22/05/9b/dd/raju-k.jpg", "contribution_count": 46, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-01", "published_at_date": "2018-10-01"}, {"review_id": 620890520, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r620890520-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Special place ", "text": "This is a special place. It’s not the most interesting or beautiful but tHis is where they clement the bodies of the dead.\nIt has a special effect on you when you these ceremonies. The place itself is nice but you cannot visit the temple.\nIt’s A point still not to miss\n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B91C8B0763EFE304993C2E97B53B4743", "name": "Ronygr", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Ronygr", "username": "Ronygr", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0b/15/54/b7/ronygr.jpg", "contribution_count": 730, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293984, "location_name": "Tel Aviv", "location_name_detailed": "Tel Aviv, Israel"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-01", "published_at_date": "2018-10-01"}, {"review_id": 620774828, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r620774828-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Hindu Temple", "text": "Pashupantinath Temple is located in North-east of Kathmandu the capital of Nepal. It is one of UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Kathmandu. It is most popular for \"Shivaratri\". Shivaratri is one of major festivals for Hindu devotees. Shivaratri is held every year in winter season and on that occasion, over 2 million of Nepalese and foreigner devotees visit the temple. In addition, it is funeral spot for Hindu people and they believe to do that in this temple.\nIt reflects traditional arts, custom, and culture. There are ancient inscriptions carved on the rock built for temple and useful buildings.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "DBB8D296F9E63BD4BE910673DAF3E39A", "name": "Nepal Mountain Kingdom", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Rai_Bimochan", "username": "Rai_Bimochan", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/18/91/17/60/rai-bimochan.jpg", "contribution_count": 15, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-30", "published_at_date": "2018-09-30"}, {"review_id": 620740721, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r620740721-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Lovely spiritual place", "text": "Lovely temple and a must visit for Hindus. Very much a spiritual and non-touristic place, good to see that they have preserved it as a peaceful place of worship for the local community instead of selling it out as a tourist attraction. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "81BBAA652E96CC60C2F92992EF2D3833", "name": "Haseena H", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/haseenah2013", "username": "haseenah2013", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a