rve the creamatory system and process of Hindus.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "01F10B5271D326EC68F2E719CFFCFB5B", "name": "Pawan S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/39pawans", "username": "39pawans", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f4/20/default-avatar-2020-31.jpg", "contribution_count": 5, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-29", "published_at_date": "2018-09-29"}, {"review_id": 620294373, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r620294373-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Amazing Place", "text": "It's a must visit in Kathmandu. Great spiritual place indeed. It was my first place to visit and I thoroughly enjoyed it.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "8997E10E2F38D5F5EC55ED463BCD3564", "name": "DJKM", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DJKM", "username": "DJKM", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/e7/default-avatar-2020-37.jpg", "contribution_count": 18, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 154996, "location_name": "Mississauga", "location_name_detailed": "Mississauga, Canada"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-28", "published_at_date": "2018-09-28"}, {"review_id": 619943898, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619943898-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Visit to Temple", "text": "If one is visiting Kathmandu, Nepal, one cannot help but visit Pashupati Nath. The feeling of serenity one gets when visiting here in remarkable. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3450C42DDDCBAEEEC82137F4B7770C95", "name": "RKSingh3007", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/RKSingh3007", "username": "RKSingh3007", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 3, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 3395996, "location_name": "Maihar", "location_name_detailed": "Maihar, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-27", "published_at_date": "2018-09-27"}, {"review_id": 619870016, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619870016-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Interesting, but not a ton to see here as a non-Hindu", "text": "The place is interesting due to its significance to those of the Hindu faith along with its age, but there is not a ton to see. It is definitely worth seeing, but it does not take that long to see even with a guide. Some might feel uncomfortable here with bodies being cremated in the open, so keep that in mind.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "777CE98C3CD3A4B555EB5E6C0C887B75", "name": "KOVH", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/KOVH", "username": "KOVH", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/14/d2/93/08/kovh.jpg", "contribution_count": 58, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-27", "published_at_date": "2018-09-27"}, {"review_id": 619606712, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619606712-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Holy Jyotirlinga", "text": "On my recent visit to Nepal, my first visit, going to Pashupatinath Temple was a given.. One of the 12 Jyotirlingas or 12 abodes Of Bhagwan Shiva is a mandatory visit for Hindus.\n\nAn ancient temple and a most prominent among Shiva Temple was an abode peace and piety.\n\nThe temple on banks of Bagmati River is a sharp contrast to similar temples we see in India. Place is clean, quiet, serene and well managed. The entrance through a massive gate forwards you to not take any photographs inside the temple. Something that I missed noticing, I dared take a snap of the massive statue of Nandi, the ride of Bhagwan Shiva. And a temple guard promptly asked me to delete the photograph.\n\nBarring that, the temple queues are well managed, orderly and quiet. \n\nIt was a very humbling e perience.\n\nTemple closes at 7 pm in evening with a Aarti on river bank. I unfortunately missed that due to some confusion. But this is as grand as the one you see at Haridwar or Varanasi", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CD26F96CCE49793232C0A7AF6D52F291", "name": "Charan63", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Charan63", "username": "Charan63", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/ef/default-avatar-2020-66.jpg", "contribution_count": 112, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554, "location_name": "Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-26", "published_at_date": "2018-09-26"}, {"review_id": 619304474, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619304474-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A Complex of Temples and Incineration Site", "text": "Hindu temples mostly dedicated to Shiva on the banks of the Bagmati River where cremations are held daily, Connected to a park, many steps, extremely interesting and spiritual even if you are not religious.  World Heritage Site, not to be missed.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "A44612EFB7116F80D1082D8742E1090E", "name": "JillSuz", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/JillSuz", "username": "JillSuz", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/f5/93/c9/jillsuz.jpg", "contribution_count": 7, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187514, "location_name": "Madrid", "location_name_detailed": "Madrid, Spain"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-25", "published_at_date": "2018-09-25"}, {"review_id": 619290814, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619290814-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A cultural experience", "text": "It was a different and moving experience to watch Hindu cremation rituals held at the Bagmati river. The main temple is strictly for Hindus only. One can ascend staircase on the opposite temple complex and have the aerial view of the Pashupatinah temple complex. There are holy men and monkeys everywhere, watch out for your personal stuff. As this is a worship place, wear appropriately.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "11F3D8090D6591BA1BB67305ADC0FA6C", "name": "TresSdk", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/TresSdk", "username": "TresSdk", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/eb/default-avatar-2020-27.jpg", "contribution_count": 128, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-25", "published_at_date": "2018-09-25"}, {"review_id": 619070108, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619070108-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Fascinating temple particularly if cremations are happening", "text": "Pashupatinath is on the banks of the river Bagmati and is a prime site for cremations. It is worth trying to ensure that you visit when cremations are taking place as it gives a fascination insight into an aspect of Hinduism not normally witnessed. There was evidence of earthquake damage and the 1000 rupee charge to get into the temple has probably been levied at that level to help with rebuild costs.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6B5CC662B06C64BC60EE934A4C5F0B44", "name": "Gina C", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/GinaC534", "username": "GinaC534", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e3/1f/default-avatar-2020-46.jpg", "contribution_count": 49, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186299, "location_name": "Southampton", "location_name_detailed": "Southampton, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-24", "published_at_date": "2018-09-24"}, {"review_id": 619012672, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r619012672-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A cultural experience", "text": "It is expensive for foreigners to enter. But worth it to experience Hindu cremation. I know it sounds ghoulish but it was an interesting cultural experience.  It was hard to watch a family saying goodbye to a loved one, then the body being burned.  If you are squeamish, don't go.  Many guides will approach you offering their services.  We chose not to get one.  We walked around the area, saw the monkeys, holy men.  All in all, it was a must see.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-06-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6BCB7A8C56C9D24649C966D36E4E74A7", "name": "ohiowanderer", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ohiowanderer", "username": "ohiowanderer", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/a0/4b/1e/ohiowanderer.jpg", "contribution_count": 1114, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 50226, "location_name": "Columbus", "location_name_detailed": "Columbus, Ohio"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-24", "published_at_date": "2018-09-24"}, {"review_id": 618368554, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r618368554-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "breathtaking place", "text": "unusual experienced i ever had, the spiritual vibe is so strong but I was really enjoy it. We have to respect the rituals. The ritual start around 5pm. Enterance fee 1000NPR. Wearing 'close' clothes.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "50999A6EF96F25DC3230DD13146067E7", "name": "dyningrum", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/dyningrum", "username": "dyningrum", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/14/c9/bb/6f/sunshine620007.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294229, "location_name": "Jakarta", "location_name_detailed": "Jakarta, Indonesia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-21", "published_at_date": "2018-09-21"}, {"review_id": 618284513, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r618284513-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "One of the must see sites ", "text": "Don't be deterred by this place being a funeral pyre site.  And above all respect the mourners.  I saw tourists gawking at the bodies and taking photos within a couple of feet away.  This is unacceptable.  You can take photos from the bridge over the river with a zoom lens.  Be aware that most of the people who want to pose for photos demand exorbitant fees.  Check out what is appropriate ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B681F38A492F37465112A7321C9F4923", "name": "Didi M", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DidiM_12", "username": "DidiM_12", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f0/9f/default-avatar-2020-16.jpg", "contribution_count": 129, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255371, "location_name": "Whangarei", "location_name_detailed": "Whangarei, New Zealand"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-09-20", "published_at_dat